From f94a4f3262d1b469df6fbf5c5b7e2b0914c873c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TAKANO Mitsuhiro <takano32@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:17:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: perf: Point the userspace counter example at an
 existing file

Documentation/arch/arm64/perf.rst tells the reader to look at
tools/perf/arch/arm64/tests/user-events.c and links to that path, but
the file does not exist: tools/perf/arch/arm64/tests/ does not contain
it, and no commit in this tree adds one.  The old link returns 404.

The userspace register access this section describes is covered by the
"User space counter reading of instructions" and "User space counter
reading of cycles" test cases in tools/perf/tests/mmap-basic.c, and
`perf test -v user` runs them.  On arm64 they request user access
through config1.  The existing example a few lines above,
tools/lib/perf/tests/test-evsel.c, is not run by `perf test`, which is
why this section points at a test that is.

Point the example and its link target at that file.

`make htmldocs` does not fetch external links, so a plain documentation
build does not catch this; `make linkcheckdocs` would.  The old link
target returns 404 and the new one returns 200.  No kernel was built.

The edit and this changelog were written with the help of an LLM
assistant (Hermes Agent); the link check above was run on the
submitter's machine.

Fixes: aa1005d15d2a ("Documentation: arm64: Document PMU counters access from userspace")
---
 Documentation/arch/arm64/perf.rst | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/arch/arm64/perf.rst b/Documentation/arch/arm64/perf.rst
index 997fd716b82f..908ea350603a 100644
--- a/Documentation/arch/arm64/perf.rst
+++ b/Documentation/arch/arm64/perf.rst
@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@ only be enabled when the tasks are pinned to a homogeneous subset of cores and
 the corresponding PMU instance is opened by specifying the 'type' attribute.
 The use of generic event types is not supported in this case.
 
-Have a look at `tools/perf/arch/arm64/tests/user-events.c`_ for an example. It
+Have a look at `tools/perf/tests/mmap-basic.c`_ for an example. It
 can be run using the perf tool to check that the access to the registers works
 correctly from userspace:
 
@@ -160,8 +160,8 @@ userspace must treat the upper 32-bits read from the counter as UNKNOWN. The
 and should be used to mask the upper bits as needed.
 
 .. Links
-.. _tools/perf/arch/arm64/tests/user-events.c:
-   https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/tools/perf/arch/arm64/tests/user-events.c
+.. _tools/perf/tests/mmap-basic.c:
+   https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/tools/perf/tests/mmap-basic.c
 .. _tools/lib/perf/tests/test-evsel.c:
    https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/tools/lib/perf/tests/test-evsel.c
 

